One in four Europeans has fallen victim to an online scam, from identity fraud to fake romances. The rise of artificial intelligence is ushering in new risks. Minh Nguyen, Chief Product Officer at security solutions provider Entrust, says both online platforms and governments can play a role in protecting consumers and businesses.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f127322-ce19-11f1-9f65-23d55109f116/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-b996a739.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f127322-ce19-11f1-9f65-23d55109f116/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-b996a739.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fd519900-cd60-11f1-979e-bf5e2231274d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:33:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Kate MOODY</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>What is happening in France? Unpacking the recent waves of protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261022-what-is-happening-in-france-unpacking-the-recent-waves-of-protests</link><description>
Laura D. Keesman, an assistant professor of sociology based in Amsterdam, analysed recent French mobilisations and the government's police response. After weekend of unrest and riots, the government acknowledged that the security response had fallen short and promised a stronger approach ahead of a new wave of protests.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5ea80a1e-ce19-11f1-a7a4-97baf3e9dd31/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-94c7ef8b.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5ea80a1e-ce19-11f1-a7a4-97baf3e9dd31/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-94c7ef8b.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0a92f57e-ce19-11f1-96c8-fb53543d2e86</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:15:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>REPLAY: French President vows to prevent violence ahead of protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261022-replay-french-president-vows-to-prevent-violence-ahead-of-protests</link><description>
French President ​Emmanuel Macron spoke to the press on Thursday after a meeting with security chiefs. He said that "illegitimate" protests would be banned in ​coming ‌days, ⁠while those from ‌organised groups such as unions ⁠would be offered alternative paths ​for the marches ‌to protect businesses.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d76a89de-cb19-11f1-8162-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3N97W4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d76a89de-cb19-11f1-8162-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3N97W4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9736799a-ce16-11f1-9fb6-f33ad219b8e6</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:04:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Entre Nous</category><title>From screen to stage: 'Singin' in the Rain' comes to Paris</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261022-from-screen-to-stage-singin-in-the-rain-comes-to-paris</link><description>
One of the most recognisable and beloved musicals of all time has hit the stage in Paris. "Singin' in the Rain" is on at the Lido theatre until January 10. In this edition of Entre Nous we are pleased to welcome Ashley Day, the British actor bringing Don Lockwood to life. He tells us what it's like to step into Gene Kelly's shoes. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c016b1b4-ce10-11f1-81b1-97baf3e9dd31/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d31a16c8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c016b1b4-ce10-11f1-81b1-97baf3e9dd31/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d31a16c8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7c58fd14-ce07-11f1-b770-add9f06acbe8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:02:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Delano D’SOUZA</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Brazil's sprawling favelas require long-term urban planning solutions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261022-brazil-s-sprawling-favelas-require-long-term-urban-planning-solutions</link><description>
As Brazilians head to the polls on Sunday for the second round of presidential elections, our correspondents take us to the heart of the country's favelas, where residents live in unsanitary conditions. Over the past 40 years, the area occupied by Brazilian favelas has almost tripled in size. They now cover around 460,000 hectares, compared with 53,700 in 1985. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0dc5c6f8-ce10-11f1-979d-3f59e19fd7f8/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e0525447.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0dc5c6f8-ce10-11f1-979d-3f59e19fd7f8/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-e0525447.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">df972616-cd6d-11f1-ada2-4ff42493b79f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:31:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marine RESSE</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France reports first human case of Shamonda virus, but says there's no public health risk</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261022-france-reports-first-human-case-of-shamonda-virus-but-says-there-s-no-public-health-risk</link><description>
France has reported the first-ever recorded case of a human contracting the Shamonda livestock virus, which is most commonly found in cattle. Public health authorities stressed that there did not appear to be any health risk to the public, adding that the infection had been "an exceptional case" involving a person with a severely compromised immune system.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c90e21c2-ce00-11f1-9ac6-23d55109f116/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25281484289422.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c90e21c2-ce00-11f1-9ac6-23d55109f116/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25281484289422.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fe771850-ce0a-11f1-a056-69ef70d39ea0</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:22:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c90e21c2-ce00-11f1-9ac6-23d55109f116/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25281484289422.jpg">© François Mori, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>Are fresh US-Israeli strikes on Iran in the pipeline?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261022-are-fresh-us-israeli-strikes-on-iran-in-the-pipeline</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, October 22: The New York Times's sources report plans for fresh strikes on Iran after the US midterm elections. In other news, the French Senate publishes a 30-step proposal for how to "take back control", just days after protests gave way to riots. Also, how software engineers found and patched up bugs in the language that makes up 70 percent of the internet. Finally, the story of a man for whom what happened in Vegas did not stay there.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/85419180-cded-11f1-b616-ab78a7fed2ce/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bd8a83d8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/85419180-cded-11f1-b616-ab78a7fed2ce/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-bd8a83d8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fcff90e8-cdeb-11f1-82ac-a5297acf9f38</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:32:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Antonia KERRIGAN</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 Live: France will ban 'illegitimate' protests in coming days, says Macron</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-live-paris-bans-protests-after-violent-unrest-as-macron-takes-swipe-at-trump</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">9b9a4d06-ce05-11f1-9084-79dd107cfa0f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:44:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>Dalai Lama appointed by China 'is going to be a fake one', exiled former Tibetan leader says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261022-dalai-lama-appointed-by-china-is-going-to-be-a-fake-one-exiled-former-tibetan-leader-says</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, exiled former Tibetan leader Lobsang Sangay said any successor to the Dalai Lama appointed by China "is going to be a fake one". He also likened Beijing's ethnic unity law to "an ethnic erasure", said Tibetan concerns had been "downgraded a bit" in US-China talks and accused China of failing to warn of the deadly August floods on the Nepal-Tibet border.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bbc18672-c7b5-11f1-a05b-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-PKG-CLEAN-TETE-A-TETE-Lobsang-Sangay-AUBIN-Sophian.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bbc18672-c7b5-11f1-a05b-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-PKG-CLEAN-TETE-A-TETE-Lobsang-Sangay-AUBIN-Sophian.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ecb91a8e-c7b4-11f1-bd29-9f686ef585fa</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:22:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 International Criminal Court wins EU's Sakharov human rights prize</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-international-criminal-court-wins-eu-s-sakharov-human-rights-prize</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">eff57f74-ce00-11f1-b9bc-51071d2db90e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:11:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>International Criminal Court wins EU's Sakharov human rights prize</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-international-criminal-court-wins-eu-s-sakharov-human-rights-prize</link><description>
The International Criminal Court, which US President Donald Trump's administration has threatened to dismantle "brick by brick", has been awarded the European Union's Sakharov human rights prize.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3c26ff2-ce00-11f1-9367-3f59e19fd7f8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-01T060027Z-1367355887-RC20XGAUF5NC-RTRMADP-3-NOBEL-PRIZE-PEACE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3c26ff2-ce00-11f1-9367-3f59e19fd7f8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-01T060027Z-1367355887-RC20XGAUF5NC-RTRMADP-3-NOBEL-PRIZE-PEACE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d8c36e56-ce00-11f1-8339-b3c7330cc5cc</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:10:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3c26ff2-ce00-11f1-9367-3f59e19fd7f8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-01T060027Z-1367355887-RC20XGAUF5NC-RTRMADP-3-NOBEL-PRIZE-PEACE.jpg">© Piroschka Van De Wouw, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Business</category><title>Meta's Zuckerberg pitches AI successes to investors with 26% rise in quarterly revenue</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261022-meta-s-zuckerberg-pitches-ai-successes-to-investors-with-26-rise-in-quarterly-revenue</link><description>
Meta Platforms CEO Mark Zuckerberg touted the company's progress on artificial intelligence during an earnings call on Wednesday and called for more investment. The tech giant's Muse AI agent has garnered 10 million users since its launch six weeks ago, while third-quarter revenue rose to $64.6 billion. Meanwhile, the company is accused of political interference in Brazil's presidential election. Also in this edition, we check in on France's rising borrowing costs.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c21a682-cded-11f1-895f-ab78a7fed2ce/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-27e5937d.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c21a682-cded-11f1-895f-ab78a7fed2ce/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-27e5937d.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2682daba-cdec-11f1-9589-8b0a3dcc1c69</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:18:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Charles PELLEGRIN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Popular dissatisfaction' across Europe: 'Promises of more economic growth haven't come true'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261022-popular-dissatisfaction-across-europe-promises-of-more-economic-growth-haven-t-come-true-1</link><description>
Oliver Farry is pleased to welcome Steven Erlanger, Chief Diplomatic Correspondent in Europe for The New York Times, based in Berlin. Europe's political centre is confronting a crisis that extends far beyond electoral volatility. From France and Germany to Italy and Spain, mounting economic frustration, generational inequality and declining confidence in established political leadership are reshaping the continent's democratic landscape. "The promises of more economic growth haven't come true," explains Erlanger, describing a continent marked by "a kind of general disgust" and "a sense of drift." 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/81ff0c2e-cdf1-11f1-a036-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261022-080451-081523-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/81ff0c2e-cdf1-11f1-a036-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261022-080451-081523-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">87e175b4-cdf1-11f1-8af1-3bbac81999a9</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:01:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Europe's wave of anger: How far will youth-led protests go?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261022-europe-s-wave-of-anger-how-far-will-youth-led-protests-go</link><description>
Youth-driven protests have been popping up all over Europe: in Belgium, Italy, Spain, Portugal, Albania, Serbia and Greece. The spark here in France was deteriorating conditions in high schools and universities, particularly for students from underprivileged backgrounds. Meanwhile, wages aren't keeping up with inflation. The housing crisis is front and centre in places like Spain and Portugal, while corruption and democratic backsliding have sparked uproar in Albania and Serbia.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edc35490-cdee-11f1-83f4-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1a79c571.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edc35490-cdee-11f1-83f4-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1a79c571.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4031c3c6-cd75-11f1-aea6-c31b41afe759</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 08:12:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Manchester United blown out of the water by Como in Champions League rout</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261022-manchester-united-blown-out-of-the-water-by-como-in-champions-league-rout</link><description>
Michael Carrick's side saw their winless run extend to seven matches in all competitions as a Nico Paz double powered the Italian side to an emphatic 4-1 win on Wednesday night. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/513b3696-cdc7-11f1-87c9-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/J24-United-Como.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/513b3696-cdc7-11f1-87c9-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/J24-United-Como.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">35fae588-cdc8-11f1-84a4-6f1621dd8a5d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 06:13:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>L'Equipe TV</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukraine’s Pavlohrad refuses to yield to Putin despite unrelenting bombardment</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-war-in-ukraine-under-bombardment-the-city-that-refuses-to-bow-to-putin</link><description>
In Pavlohrad, a Ukrainian city less than 90km from the front line with Russia, there is no respite from war. Residents describe daily life under bombardment, caught between exhaustion and determination. Amid criticism of Trump, TikTok rumours and strikes against civilians, FRANCE 24 gathered accounts from those who “refuse to yield”.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/19814b0a-cd36-11f1-86ec-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/20261020-115807996-iOS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/19814b0a-cd36-11f1-86ec-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/20261020-115807996-iOS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7a651c96-cd6b-11f1-a92d-133a2e5ab8f8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 05:54:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/19814b0a-cd36-11f1-86ec-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/20261020-115807996-iOS.jpg">© Assiya Hamza, FRANCE 24</source><dc:creator>Assiya HAMZA</dc:creator></item><item><category>Technology</category><title>'Backbone of the web': What is PHP and how has it raised AI hacking fears?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20261022-backbone-of-the-web-what-is-php-and-how-has-it-raised-ai-hacking-fears</link><description>
As governments and corporations alike scramble to install a patch to fix fundamental security flaws in a programming language that helps run roughly 70 percent of the world's websites, here's what you need to know about how AI has helped bring these critical vulnerabilities to light.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8a62bfea-cdcf-11f1-835f-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/17d20d48dd7c35c2a22cd35c79d7522fecda4d4e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8a62bfea-cdcf-11f1-835f-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/17d20d48dd7c35c2a22cd35c79d7522fecda4d4e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8b15bc3a-cdcf-11f1-b8bf-b3d0b1fa4ef0</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 04:17:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8a62bfea-cdcf-11f1-835f-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/17d20d48dd7c35c2a22cd35c79d7522fecda4d4e.jpg">© Kirill Kudryavtsev, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: France will ban 'illegitimate' protests in coming days, says Macron</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-live-paris-bans-protests-after-violent-unrest-as-macron-takes-swipe-at-trump</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron said on Thursday that "illegitimate" protests would be banned in the coming days, ⁠while those from organised groups such as unions would be offered alternative paths for the marches to protect businesses. The government has said it will put French soldiers in the street after rioting and looting broke out on the fringes of mass peaceful demonstrations over the weekend. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/885ffc7c-cb9e-11f1-9658-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26290455197328.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/885ffc7c-cb9e-11f1-9658-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26290455197328.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c9855b30-cd9b-11f1-b30f-1554c3daca68</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 02:28:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/885ffc7c-cb9e-11f1-9658-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26290455197328.jpg">© Laurent Cipriani, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia and Ukraine trade strikes overnight as Moscow signals readiness for peace talks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-russia-missiles-kyiv-ukraine-peace-talks</link><description>
Russia and Ukraine traded major drone and missile strikes on each other's capitals overnight, hours after Moscow signalled readiness to resume US-mediated peace talks. President Donald Trump said negotiations were closer than ever to ending the war, though the Kremlin expressed doubts over Ukrainian and European proposals.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bf71a96e-cb7f-11f1-8810-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-18T235422Z-1304641961-RC2X5OA93ZJS-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bf71a96e-cb7f-11f1-8810-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-18T235422Z-1304641961-RC2X5OA93ZJS-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">80800f1a-cdba-11f1-9a55-a11dad8efa18</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 01:51:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bf71a96e-cb7f-11f1-8810-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-18T235422Z-1304641961-RC2X5OA93ZJS-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg">© Valentyn Ogirenko, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ireland votes to end UN approval requirement for overseas peacekeeping missions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-ireland-votes-un-veto-overseas-peacekeeping-missions</link><description>
Irish lawmakers voted Wednesday to scrap a requirement for UN approval before deploying military peacekeepers overseas, approving the controversial legislation by 79 votes to 71. Opposition lawmakers warned the move threatened Ireland’s longstanding military neutrality. Ireland is not a NATO member but has traditionally participated in international peacekeeping missions.
